[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105186,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Phakomatous choristoma is a benign congenital developmental lesion of the lens placode, composed of extraocular crystalline lens tissue and its basement membrane.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:24:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105187,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:24:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105188,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LA14.0Y Other specified structural developmental anomalies of eyelids</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:24:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105189,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> Zimmerman tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:24:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105190,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:24:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105191,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesion generally occurs deep in the medial lower eyelid, but cases with exclusive involvement of the inferior anterior orbit have been reported {30407999; 10406159}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:24:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105192,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with a smooth, firm, slowly growing subcutaneous mass in the medial lower eyelid, already present at birth.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:24:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105193,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Phakomatous choristoma is extremely rare, with &lt;&nbsp;30&nbsp;cases reported worldwide.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:24:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105194,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This is a developmental abnormality.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:24:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105195,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Two hypotheses have been proposed as to the origin of the lesion: the formation of an additional lens vesicle locus {5542122}, and the displacement or migration of cells from the lens placode {973823; 16102745}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:24:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105196,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>They are composed of pale, firm, round tissue and are as large as 20&nbsp;mm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:24:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105197,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The histological appearance is typical and consists of desmoplastic-like stroma with islands of cuboid to polygonal cells surrounded by a thick layer of eosinophilic, amorphic, PAS-positive material analogous to lens capsule. Other features are the presence of bladder/Wedl-like cells and psammomatous calcification {5542122}. The epithelioid cells stain positively for vimentin, S100, and lens crystalline proteins and are negative for cytokeratins. Electron microscopy reveals 10&nbsp;nm whorled cytoplasmic microfilaments within degenerating epithelial cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:24:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105198,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:24:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105199,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:24:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105200,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> orbital/eyelid localization; extraocular crystalline lens tissue and dense collagen bundles surrounded by a PAS-positive membrane.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:24:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105201,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:24:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105202,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Phakomatous choristoma is benign; malignant transformation has not been described. Simple resection is sufficient; recurrences have not been reported. The ipsilateral eye is typically normal. However, a case of a myopic eye with a colobomatous hypoplastic optic disc and staphyloma has been reported {16424545}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-07-13T16:24:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]